id: pm-2qqcgl
title: "The coverage gate every contributor is told to run is not a gate: run-tests.mjs coverage prints the shortfall and exits 0, so only CI can fail on coverage"
description: ""
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[4]: agent-ux,ci,coverage,gate-parity
created_at: "2026-08-05T18:43:54.168Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-06T06:55:37.571Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#fd4660418d2b99c9f530a6e2"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "The documented local coverage command exits non-zero on the same condition the hosted threshold step rejects; The failure message names the files below threshold and their uncovered lines, so a contributor can act without opening a CI log; The threshold values have a single declared source shared by the local command and the hosted step, rather than being restated in each; A negative control proves the local command can fail on a deliberately uncovered branch"
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: high
confidence: high
expected_result: The command AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md name as the coverage gate fails locally on exactly the condition the hosted global-threshold step fails on.
actual_result: "node scripts/run-tests.mjs coverage passes --coverage to vitest and nothing else. On 2026-08-05 it printed 'All files | 100 | 99.99 | 100 | 100' and exited 0. The hosted Gates (coverage) job then failed its separate 'Merge coverage and enforce global thresholds' step on the identical number: 'ERROR: Coverage for branches (99.99%) does not meet global threshold (100%)'. The shortfall was three unreachable nullish fallbacks in one file at 98.5 percent branches."
